Title: 200 AMSTERDAM: THE VERTICAL CITY
Credit: Written for the Screen by
Author: Danny Bouldiez
Episode: PART 02: WARM WIND (CHAPTER 01)

====

EXT. WEST ANTARCTIC ICE SHEET - NIGHT

An eerie, bruised-violet AURORA pulses across the frozen sky. Charged particles stream through the upper ionosphere.

INT. WAIS FIELD STATION - CONTINUOUS

NIKO (38, magnetospheric physicist) and ASTRID (40s, Norwegian glaciologist) stand illuminated by three glowing monitors.

                         NIKO
          The column is dropping fast enough to trigger every 
          alarm we have. Energetic-particle chemistry is producing 
          odd nitrogen in the upper atmosphere. But that cannot 
          explain the heat signal at the ice-bed interface.

                         ASTRID
          The hydraulic wedge from the seventh circle of hell. 
          The basal-pressure network says the decoupled area is 
          expanding inland at meters per hour!

Niko taps the geodetic residual graph. A synchronized red waveform pulses across the screen: 0.05 Hz.

                         NIKO
          Look at the spectral line. Tokyo. Reykjavik. São Paulo. 
          And Manhattan. Sensors thousands of miles apart are 
          acquiring the exact same harmonic frequency.

                         ASTRID
          What is generating a synchronized frequency across 
          the entire crust of the Earth?

                         NIKO
          Not what. Where. The telluric currents are converging 
          on the oldest metamorphic granite on the Atlantic coast. 
          New York City.

SOUND: A low, infrasonic HUM builds, vibrating the ice beneath their boots.

FADE TO BLACK.
